sub:assertion {
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/morphoeval-delphi10000-drosophila-berryi-turing-wavelength-s0> pk:hasAssessment <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-drosophila-berryi-turing-wavelength-s0-overall> .
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-drosophila-berryi-turing-wavelength-s0-overall> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
        rdfs:label "Drosophila berryi detail-scale Turing wavelength at 1.754 µm (19 Ma) — MorphoEval overall 83.1/100" ;
        dct:date "2026-10-27"^^xsd:date ;
        dct:description "Pass 1 Schnakenberg model of the Drosophila berryi detail-scale Turing wavelength. Classical lambda_c is calibrated to 1.754 µm at 19 Ma. Modal growth rates match the Jacobian eigenvalue with Pearson r = 0.999998 and RMSE = 0.000250. The chronoseries at fixed mode number N = 55.87 shortens from 2.040 µm (succini, 44 Ma) to 1.754 µm (berryi) to 1.718 µm (affinis, 0 Ma). Equal-diffusion and u^2 v ablation both decay, but the equal-diffusion rate is not yet quantitative. The gallery plate is an amber spiral, not a 1.8 µm micrograph. Overall 83.1/100 (faithfulness 81.4, reproducibility 86.9); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit 0c76d15d14afcec6c366e1b9274a6586a0de48fc; environment: python 3.12.3, numpy 2.5.4, scipy 1.18.1, matplotlib 3.11.2, Pillow 13.0.0. Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 86, Morphological realism / specimen match 76, Parameter expressivity 82, Morphometric validation 84, Source and data traceability 88, Code-to-model traceability 84, Reproducibility package 88. Output judged: docs/media/drosophila_berryi_turing_wavelength_s0_comparison.png: rendered output of models/2026-delphi10000-drosophila-berryi-turing-wavelength-s0.py at 0c76d15d14afcec6c366e1b9274a6586a0de48fc, image/png, 430729 B, 1344×1008 px, artifact_sha256 564dff560a1b2d9d7bec91135151ea24c374b44caa584a46fa509c84978ff2fa (sha256 564dff560a1b2d9d7bec91135151ea24c374b44caa584a46fa509c84978ff2fa), spec_fingerprint fe2e74bbe1194adf9f66d7de47fdd4b5119a2272757767687404f3140401fa54. Dual provenance: spec_fingerprint: fe2e74bbe1194adf9f66d7de47fdd4b5119a2272757767687404f3140401fa54; artifact_sha256: 564dff560a1b2d9d7bec91135151ea24c374b44caa584a46fa509c84978ff2fa. Claim boundary: reported_in_source: Turing 1952 dispersion relation and the critical-wavenumber condition for a two-species reaction-diffusion system. | Schnakenberg 1979 kinetics f = a - u + u^2 v, g = b - u^2 v. | Grimaldi 1987 monograph of Hispaniolan amber Drosophilidae; Grimaldi 1995 on the Miocene age of Dominican amber.; reconstructed_in_script: Berryi detail-scale parameters a=0.2305, b=0.7942, D_u=0.03686, D_v=1.721, with the spatial unit set so classical lambda_c is 1.754 µm. | Chronoseries detail wavelengths 2.040, 1.754 and 1.718 µm obtained by dividing catalogued tissue stripes 114, 98 and 96 µm by the fixed mode number 98/1.754. | Modal growth rates from a semi-implicit Fourier step compared with the Jacobian eigenvalue.; transfer_boundary: The 19 Ma / 44 Ma / 0 Ma ages and the tissue wavelengths are Project Delphi chronoseries assignments, not measurements quoted from Grimaldi 1987. | Murray 1981 is the scale argument for a chemical wavelength riding on a changing domain metric, transferred from vertebrate coat markings to an amber drosophilid.; does_not_claim: That Grimaldi 1987 measured a 1.754 µm pigment wavelength. | That the gallery JPEG is a micrograph of berryi ocellar pigment at 1.8 µm. | That the GIF terminal frame is an unprocessed PDE field; it crossfades onto the gallery plate for the image-fitness crop.." ;
        dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-rubric-0.1.0> ;
        pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> ;
        pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/overall" ;
        pk:evidenceAgainst "remediation needed: {'id': 'R1', 'item': 'Equal-diffusion control matches the sign of sigma but not the rate (-1.32 measured vs -0.41 eigenvalue). Refit with a smaller step and an earlier window.'}",
            "remediation needed: {'id': 'R2', 'item': 'Late-time nonlinear coarsening of the 2D Schnakenberg field is not measured against lambda_sigma.'}",
            "remediation needed: {'id': 'R3', 'item': 'No second assessor. The gallery plate is not a 1.8 µm fossil micrograph; keep that limit explicit rather than raising specimen-match to match the GIF crop score.'}" ;
        pk:hasScore "0.831"^^xsd:double ;
        pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> a pk:Model ;
        rdfs:label "Grok 4.7 (builder-assessor, single-agent; second assessor not run)" ;
        dct:identifier "grok-4.7" ;
        prov:actedOnBehalfOf <https://orcid.org/0009-0007-4948-9192> .
}

